course: dictionary
lesson: 1280
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. «Mum bought sausages and mince at the butcher's.» Here butcher's is a shop, the place where meat is sold.
explain: «The butcher cut the meat into chops.» Here butcher is a person, whose job is cutting and selling meat. Butcher can also be a verb: to butcher an animal means to kill it and cut it up for meat.
explain: The word can be used in a joking way too. «He butchered that song» does not mean he cut up a song; it means he spoiled it badly. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: A butcher is a person whose job is cutting and selling meat.
fact: The butcher's is the shop where meat is sold.
fact: To butcher an animal means to kill it and cut it up for meat.
fact: In informal speech, «butchered» can mean spoiled badly, as in «He butchered that song».
fact: In UK rhyming slang, «butcher's hook» means look, so «have a butcher's» means «have a look».
exercise: «Mum bought sausages and mince at the butcher's.» Where did Mum buy the meat? | At the library, for a book | At the bakery, for bread | *At the butcher's shop | At the bank, to save money
exercise: «He butchered that song.» What does butchered mean here? | Sang it very loudly | *Spoiled it badly | Cut it into pieces for dinner | Wrote it down neatly
exercise: In London, Sam says, «Have a butcher's at this!» What does he mean? | A sharp knife to cut with | *Have a look | Have a rest | Have a meat pie
test: Which word means a person whose job is cutting and selling meat? | Chef | Farmer | *Butcher | Baker
test: Which sentence uses butcher in its informal meaning, spoiled badly? | *«He butchered that song» | Mum went to the butcher's on Friday | The butcher's shop was closed | The butcher cut the chops
exam: Jo reads, «Dad said he would have a butcher's at the photos.» What does have a butcher's mean? | To spoil the photos badly | To cut the photos into pieces | *To have a look | To buy some meat
